    "question": {
      ":question/id": "90e356f1-9a22-5bde-b749-373ae3d86f45",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\,\\sin\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=15^\\circ$ and then with $x=30^\\circ$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=15^\\circ$ and then at $x=30^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
